## PART 2 — What Each Sensor Is Expected to Check
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Every sensor in aviation software must guard against three types of bad data:

  CORRUPT  — the value is physically impossible (outside the valid range)
  STALE    — the sensor has stopped sending updates (no new data for too long)
  DEBOUNCE — the value is jumping/noisy (large sudden changes need confirmation)

