The analyzer read every comparison operator (<, <=, >, >=) in the sensor
code and checked whether the numeric values match what the YAML requires.

Legend:
  ✓ IMPLEMENTED    — found in the code with the correct value
  ✗ MISSING        — no comparison found at all
  ⚠ MISMATCH       — found a comparison but with a different value than YAML
  ~ INCONCLUSIVE   — found a comparison but could not confirm the exact value
  - NOT CONFIGURED — the YAML has no value to check against
  ○ DISABLED       — this check is intentionally turned off in the YAML

